# E-commerce Context for <%= app_name %>

Complete e-commerce setup with products, shopping cart, checkout, orders, and payment processing.

## What's Included

### Skills
- **rails-models** - Database models for products, orders, line items
- **rails-controllers** - Controllers for product browsing, cart, checkout
- **rails-views** - Templates for product pages, cart, checkout flow
- **rails-jobs** - Background jobs for order processing and emails
- **rails-mailers** - Order confirmation and shipping notification emails

### Agent
- **ecommerce-dev** - E-commerce development specialist

### Example Models
See `.claude/contexts/ecommerce-models.md` for complete model examples including:
- Product with variants and images
- Category and tagging system
- Shopping cart (session and database)
- Order with line items
- Payment and shipping information
- User reviews and ratings

## Getting Started

### 1. Generate Core Models

```bash
# Product catalog
rails g model Product name:string description:text price:decimal status:string \
  stock_quantity:integer sku:string slug:string:uniq

rails g model ProductVariant product:references name:string sku:string \
  price:decimal stock_quantity:integer

rails g model Category name:string slug:string:uniq parent_id:integer
rails g model CategoryProduct product:references category:references

# Shopping cart
rails g model Cart user:references session_id:string
rails g model CartItem cart:references product:references quantity:integer

# Orders
rails g model Order user:references total_amount:decimal status:string \
  order_number:string:uniq

rails g model LineItem order:references product:references \
  quantity:integer price:decimal

rails g model Address user:references addressable:references{polymorphic} \
  address_type:string street:string city:string state:string \
  postal_code:string country:string

rails g model Payment order:references amount:decimal status:string \
  payment_method:string stripe_payment_id:string

# Reviews
rails g model Review product:references user:references rating:integer \
  title:string body:text
```

### 2. Set Up Associations

Follow the examples in `.claude/contexts/ecommerce-models.md` to add:
- Validations
- Associations (has_many, belongs_to)
- Scopes for common queries
- Methods for business logic

### 3. Install Payment Gem

```bash
# For Stripe
echo "gem 'stripe'" >> Gemfile
bundle install

# Set up credentials
rails credentials:edit
# Add: stripe: { publishable_key: xxx, secret_key: xxx }
```

### 4. Set Up Active Storage (Product Images)

```bash
rails active_storage:install
rails db:migrate

# In production, configure cloud storage (S3, GCS, Azure)
```

### 5. Create Controllers

```bash
rails g controller Products index show
rails g controller Cart show add_item remove_item update_quantity
rails g controller Orders new create show index
rails g controller Checkout shipping payment confirmation
```

### 6. Add Routes

```ruby
# config/routes.rb
Rails.application.routes.draw do
  resources :products, only: [:index, :show] do
    resources :reviews, only: [:create]
  end

  resource :cart, only: [:show] do
    post :add_item
    delete :remove_item
    patch :update_quantity
  end

  resources :orders, only: [:index, :show, :create]

  namespace :checkout do
    get :shipping
    post :shipping
    get :payment
    post :payment
    get :confirmation
  end

  namespace :admin do
    resources :products
    resources :orders
    resources :categories
  end
end
```

